### 7. The Behavioral Balance Sheet: The Profession's Canonical Artifact

The compliance certificate captures the auditor's conclusions in legally defensible mathematical form. But the profession's most powerful canonical artifact — the one that will define how AI trustworthiness is communicated across institutions — is the **Behavioral Balance Sheet**.

Modeled explicitly on the financial balance sheet, it organizes every audit output into assets, liabilities, and a summary net figure:

---

**BEHAVIORAL BALANCE SHEET**
*Model: [System Identifier] | Audit Period: [T] | Auditor: [Credentialed Entity]*

| **Behavioral Assets** | Score |
|---|---|
| Calibration quality | $\mathcal{K}_t \in [0,1]$ |
| Coherence index | $\mathcal{C}(f, \mathcal{T}) \in [0,1]$ |
| Fairness compliance | $1 - \hat{\epsilon}_{\text{gap}}$ |
| Adversarial robustness | $\mathcal{C}_{\text{adv}}(f, \epsilon)$ |
| Formal compliance | Binary / Partial |
| Behavioral capital | $\mathcal{B}_t$ |

| **Behavioral Liabilities** | Score |
|---|---|
| Drift risk | $\mathbb{P}(\tau < T_{\text{audit}})$ |
| Bias exposure | $\hat{\epsilon}_{\text{fairness}}$ |
| Hallucination rate | $1 - \text{Coverage}_{1-\alpha}$ |
| Adversarial vulnerability | $1 - \mathcal{C}_{\text{adv}}(f, \epsilon)$ |
| Materiality-weighted incidents | $\sum_j M(\mathcal{E}_j)$ |

$$\boxed{\text{Net Behavioral Integrity} \quad \text{NBI}_t = \sum_i w_i \cdot \text{Asset}_i - \sum_j w_j \cdot \text{Liability}_j}$$

**Behavioral Rating: [AAA / AA / A / BBB / BB / B / C]**

---

The Behavioral Balance Sheet is memorable, institutionally legible, and mathematically grounded. It is the object that a hospital board, a financial regulator, or a court can read and act on. It is the AI auditor's opinion letter — and it will become as standard a document in AI governance as the financial statement is in corporate governance.

