### 10. Conclusion

The AI Behavior Auditor is not a role within existing professions. It is the founding specialization of an entirely new professional field — Computational Assurance Engineering — whose emergence is as structurally inevitable as the emergence of financial auditing after the industrial revolution or aviation safety inspection after powered flight.

This dissertation builds everything the profession requires to function with genuine authority: the mathematical tools that produce defensible certificates, the institutional principles that make those certificates trustworthy, the canonical artifacts that make them legible, and the liability framework that makes them consequential.

The Behavioral Balance Sheet. The Behavioral Rating. AI Materiality Theory. Behavioral Capital. Continuous Assurance. The Independence Principle. Adversarial Auditing. Auditability-by-Design.

None of these exist yet as formal professional concepts. All of them will be necessary. This dissertation makes them rigorous — at the precise historical moment when the profession that requires them is about to come into existence.

