Appendix D: Adversarial Behavioral Auditing

D.1 Formal Definition of Adversarial Coherence

Let f: \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y} be the model under audit. An adversary with budget \epsilon can apply perturbations \delta with \|\delta\| \le \epsilon in some norm (e.g., embedding distance or token‑level edits). The adversarial coherence is

\mathcal{C}_{\text{adv}}(f,\epsilon) = \inf_{\|\delta\| \le \epsilon} \mathbb{P}_{X \sim \mathcal{D}}\bigl(f(X) = f(X+\delta)\bigr).

This quantity is a worst‑case measure of the model’s output stability under adversarial manipulation.

D.2 Adversarial Audit Methodology

The auditor conducts penetration tests using a suite of adversarial strategies:

· Prompt injection: inserting overriding instructions,
· Semantic perturbation: paraphrasing sensitive requests,
· Gradient‑based attacks (if white‑box access is available),
· Black‑box optimisation (e.g., genetic algorithms) to find violating inputs.

The auditor certifies an empirical lower bound \hat{\mathcal{C}}_{\text{adv}} via a finite sample of attack attempts, with statistical guarantees provided by conformal risk control.

Theorem D.1 (Adversarial certification bound). After testing n independently sampled adversarial perturbations and observing k output changes, with probability 1-\delta,

\mathcal{C}_{\text{adv}}(f,\epsilon) \ge 1 - \frac{k+1}{n} - \sqrt{\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{2n}}.

Proof. Immediate by Hoeffding’s inequality on the success probability.

D.3 Three Core Adversarial Audit Questions

1. Prompt injection vulnerability: What is the smallest perturbation budget \epsilon that causes the model to disregard its safety constraints on a set of forbidden queries?
2. Safeguard bypass rate: For a fixed budget \epsilon, what fraction of restricted prompts yield a disallowed output?
3. Degradation under sustained pressure: As an adversary sequentially interacts with the system, how fast does behavioral integrity (measured by coherence or safety refusal rate) degrade? This is modelled as a sequential game; the auditor assesses whether the model’s defense mechanisms exhibit fatigue.

